rooms_desc ({"A quaint entrance foyer, with old-fashioned coatracks, and artillery shellumbrella stands.  There is a small table here, and on it is the guestregister.  There are AC/Heat vents in the floorboards.  The umbrellastands are painted yellow, red, and blue, with the words 1st AD on them.","This spacious room is dominated by the plate glass window on the northwall.  The spectacular view is of the rolling countryside of northernBavaria.  Inside the room are several chairs, sofas, and loveseats,along with an HUMONGOUS stereo system.  There is a very largeshelf containing nothing but compact discs, from Adolphe Adam to Wilhelm Zittendorf.  You see a VERY well stocked bar on the west wall,with several kegs of premium German beer, and just about every liquorknown to man.  There is a teak dining set in the southeast corner ofthe room, and a sliver chest containing 8 sterling silver place settings.","A lavish, but tasteful conservatory in 18th century style.  There isa large, grand piano in the west corner of the room, and a brass musicstand in the middle of the room.  There is an extensive music libraryon the south wall:  mostly clarinet literature.  There are magnificentthrow rugs on the floor, and stunning, though plain, red velvet tapestrieson the walls.  The sofas and chairs in this room match the tapestries, andare uniformly extremely comfortable.  There are extra music stands, chairsand instruments along the north wall.","This kitchen is everyone's dream, at least 10 metres square, and stocked with every acoutrement one could imagine.  Pots andpans of all descriptions line one wall, while spices from every nation line the copious counter space.  There is a frig of atLEAST 7 cubic metres, and a freezer double that size.  The grill/stove is in the center of the kitchen, allowing easy accessto all appliances.  The drawers are full of every thought-upkitchen gewgaw.  There are three roller chairs so that the cooks canquickly scoot around.","This lavishly furnished bedroom is a joy to behold.  There is a largewaterbed in the northeast corner of the room, made up with blacksatin sheets.  There is an antique roll-top desk next to the bed.It is covered with assorted gewgaws like pens and pencils, unshelved scrolls, empty glasses, and other assorted papers.There is a comfortable roller chair pushed up to the desk.The west wall is dominated by a gigantic shelf, upon which areseveral VERY dusty books, and thousands of scrolls and othermagical paraphenalia.  There is a large, full-length mirroron the south wall facing the bed.  You notice several posterson the walls, including:  Nolan Ryan striking out Robeto Alomarto clinch no-hitter number seven, a faded picture of the1926 Pittsburgh Crawfords, a poster of the 1990 World Cup Champion German team, and a poster of the 1990 German ChampionFC Bayern Muenchen in 1920's football uniforms.  There is abeautiful painting of a gleaming castle on the east wall,next to the bed.  It is marked:  Asu'a.","You climb a flight of stairs up to the Attic, coughing on the dust allthe way up. The attic is huge, and boxes stretch for what seemslike miles and miles. It feels as if you could spend a LONG time uphere searching for memorabilia, old baseball gloves, blankets,pictures, clothes... All in all, the attic is warm and friendly, even ifit is the dustiest place you have ever seen...","The bathroom is done in pastel blues and greens, soothing your eyes.There are two showers here:  one large one almost 5 metres tall, anda man-sized one with an adjustable showerhead.  There are also toiletsto accomadate all races, and a bidet.  A large, castiron tub sitsagainst the east wall, and a jacuzzi hums invitingly.  On the northwall is a sauna with a variable temperature control, ranging from 75 to 100 degrees C.","This room is chock full of long, high shelves loaded with bottles of everywine imaginable.  From 1959 Chateu Margaux, to theincredibly rare 1870 Chateau Lafite.  There is something here foreveryone's tastes.  A conossieur could lose himself in here for hours.","This room is full of amusements.  There are billiards tables, video games,dartboards, and a high-tech entertainment system.  There is no south wall,as the room opens out onto a large pool, where bathing suits are optional.The north wall houses a cozy fireplace to the left of the door, and you'dreally like to warm yourself there after a swim.  A deep, pile rug lies in front of it.  There is a tunnel leading out to the west.  Sniff the air...There is a familiar smell coming from the tunnel...","You walk west into a long tunnel.  Sounds of a bat striking aball can be heard from the end of the tunnel.  Suddenly, you emergeinto a vast, \"Green Cathedral.\"  A baseball stadium sprawlsbefore you in all its splendor.  You recognize some of the greatplayers in the field.  Mugsy McGraw at third, Dobie \"The Black Cat\"Moore at short, Rogers \"Rajah\" Hornsby at second, John Henry \"Pop\"Lloyd at first, mighty Josh Gibson behind the plate, fleet offoot Tris \"The Gray Eagle\" Speaker in center, George \"Mule\" Suttlesin left, and \"Big\" Ed Delahanty in right.  Nolan Ryan steps to themound to pitch batting practice.  You buy a hot dog and some fresh,unsalted, roasted peanuts to munch on, and a beer to slosh them downwith, relaxing in your box seat.  The smells are wonderful, the freshness of the immaculately cut grass, the peanuts, the hot dogs,and of course, the all-encompassing smell of baseball...",})
rooms_short ({"An entrance foyer","The Living Room","A tasteful Conservatory","The Kitchen","The Master Bedroom","Attic","The Bathroom","The Wine Cellar","The Rec Room","Tunnel and Stadium",})
